l's financial edge.", "watch": "Whether independent polls in October continue to show Hamilton ahead or Marshall reconsolidates Republican voters amid fading GOP enthusiasm.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Roger Marshall (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Kansas has not elected a Democratic senator in decades, and incumbent Roger Marshall begins with the structural advantage of an eight-point Republican state lean plus a large cash-on-hand lead. Yet the race has tightened dramatically: the most recent live-caller poll shows Adam Hamilton slightly ahead, and polling averages across the cycle sit near even. A former Republican governor has crossed party lines to endorse Hamilton, and national outlets describe Marshall as visibly endangered.\n\nExpert raters still mostly call the race Lean Republican, with a couple moving it to Tossup, and prediction markets continue to price Hamilton as an underdog near one-in-three. The combination of a hostile environment for the incumbent and Kansas's partisan baseline points to a narrow Republican edge with genuine upset potential.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2893, "margin": -2.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3585, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4222, "margin": -1.5}]}